🔹 5️⃣ WORD LADDER
📌 Problem Statement

You are given:

beginWord

endWord

wordList

Each transformation:

Changes only one character

Resulting word must exist in wordList

Return the length of the shortest transformation sequence from beginWord to endWord.
If not possible, return 0.

📌 Example
beginWord = "hit"
endWord   = "cog"
wordList  = ["hot","dot","dog","lot","log","cog"]

Output: 5


Sequence:

hit → hot → dot → dog → cog

💡 Key Insight

This is a shortest path problem where:

Each word = node

One-letter change = edge

All edges have equal weight

👉 Use BFS, not DFS.

🧠 Optimization Trick (Interview Gold)

Instead of comparing each word with every other word:

For each word, generate patterns:

h*t, hi*, *it


Use a HashMap<pattern, list of words>

⚙️ Algorithm (BFS)

Add beginWord to word list

Preprocess wildcard patterns

BFS from beginWord

Stop when endWord is reached

🧩 Java Code (Clean + Efficient)
class Solution {
    public int ladderLength(String beginWord, String endWord, List<String> wordList) {
        Set<String> set = new HashSet<>(wordList);
        if (!set.contains(endWord)) return 0;

        Queue<String> q = new LinkedList<>();
        q.add(beginWord);

        Set<String> visited = new HashSet<>();
        visited.add(beginWord);

        int level = 1;

        while (!q.isEmpty()) {
            int size = q.size();
            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
                String word = q.poll();
                if (word.equals(endWord)) return level;

                for (int j = 0; j < word.length(); j++) {
                    char[] arr = word.toCharArray();
                    for (char c = 'a'; c <= 'z'; c++) {
                        arr[j] = c;
                        String next = new String(arr);

                        if (set.contains(next) && !visited.contains(next)) {
                            visited.add(next);
                            q.add(next);
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            level++;
        }
        return 0;
    }
}

🧪 Dry Run (Key Levels)
Level 1: hit
Level 2: hot
Level 3: dot, lot
Level 4: dog, log
Level 5: cog ✅

⏱️ Time & Space Complexity
Type	Complexity
Time	O(N × L × 26)
Space	O(N)

👉 N = words, L = word length

🎯 Interview Tips

Always say “BFS gives shortest path”

Mention visited set

Say all transformations equal cost
